/**
 * @file operators.h
 * @brief Detailed documentation for the operators module within the AnalysisG.pyc framework, including its CUDA kernel implementations for optimized mathematical and logical operations.
 *
 * @page operators_page operators
 *
 * @section operators_intro Introduction
 * The `operators` module provides a suite of optimized mathematical and logical operators, implemented with Cython and accelerated using CUDA kernels. These operators are designed to perform common computational tasks with high efficiency, particularly beneficial for large-scale data processing and numerical simulations within the AnalysisG framework.
 *
 * @section operators_contents Contents
 * This module contains optimized operator functions, many of which leverage CUDA for parallel execution on GPUs. Specific contents will be detailed as they are implemented, highlighting their GPU-accelerated nature where applicable.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Dot(torch::Tensor* v1, torch::Tensor* v2)
 * @brief Computes the dot product between two tensors.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Cross(torch::Tensor* v1, torch::Tensor* v2)
 * @brief Computes the cross product between two 3D vector tensors.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Determinant(torch::Tensor* matrix)
 * @brief Calculates the determinant of a batch of square matrices.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::CosTheta(torch::Tensor* v1, torch::Tensor* v2)
 * @brief Computes the cosine of the angle between two tensors.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::SinTheta(torch::Tensor* v1, torch::Tensor* v2)
 * @brief Computes the sine of the angle between two tensors.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Pi_2(torch::Tensor* trn)
 * @brief Ensures angular boundaries remain within `-pi` and `pi`.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Rx(torch::Tensor* angle)
 * @brief Generates a 3D rotation matrix around the X-axis for a given angle.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Ry(torch::Tensor* angle)
 * @brief Generates a 3D rotation matrix around the Y-axis for a given angle.
 *
 * @fn torch::Tensor operators_::Rz(torch::Tensor* angle)
 * @brief Generates a 3D rotation matrix around the Z-axis for a given angle.
 *
 * @fn std::tuple<torch::Tensor, torch::Tensor> operators_::Inverse(torch::Tensor* matrix)
 * @brief Computes the inverse of a batch of square matrices.
 * @return A tuple containing the inverse matrix and a boolean tensor indicating invertibility.
 *
 * @fn std::tuple<torch::Tensor, torch::Tensor> operators_::Eigenvalue(torch::Tensor* matrix)
 * @brief Computes the eigenvalues and eigenvectors for a batch of matrices.
 * @return A tuple containing the eigenvalues and the corresponding eigenvectors.
 */
